quran[6]{c,v,t}:
  2,164,"Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth; in the alternation of night and day; in the ships that sail upon the seas with cargoes beneficial to people; in the water which Allah sends down from the sky and with which He revives the earth after its death, and scatters therein all kinds of creatures; in the changing of the winds and in the clouds that are driven between the sky and the earth: Surely there are signs (of Allah’s Power) in all of these (things) for the people who understand."
  2,165,"Still, there are some who set up equals with Allah (in worship), loving them like the love of Allah, but the believers are more ardent in loving Allah. And if the wrongdoers could see (the horrors of the Hereafter) as they will see when they face the punishment, that power belongs to Allah. And that Allah is severe in punishment."
  2,166,"(Consider the Day) when those (leaders of misguidance) who were followed will disown the followers, when they face the punishment, and all their bonds (which now unite them) will break asunder."
  2,167,"And when those (polytheists) who follow will say: ‘Had there been another turn (of worldly life) for us, we would disown them as they have disowned us now.’ Thus, Allah will show them their deeds as sources of regret for themselves. However, they shall never come out of the Fire."
  2,168,"O people! Eat from what is lawful and pure on the earth. And do not follow Satan’s footsteps, for he is your sworn enemy."
  2,169,He only incites you to commit evil and indecency and that you attribute to Allah what you do not know.
